      },
      "message": "Help\n  • The assumption h has shape “∃ n > 0, ...”\n    One can use it with:\n    Since ∃ n > 0, P n we get n such that (n_pos : n > 0) and (hn : P n)\n    The names n, n_pos and hn can be chosen freely among available names."
    },
    {
      "range": {
        "end": {
          "character": 8,
          "line": 7
        },
        "start": {
          "character": 2,
          "line": 7
        }
      },
      "message": "Help\n  • The assumption h starts with “∀ n, ...”\n    One can use it with:\n    Since ∀ (n : ℕ), P n ⇒ Q n we get that P n₀ ⇒ Q n₀\n    where n₀ is a natural number\n  • If this assumption won't be used again in its general shape, one can also specialize h with\n    We apply h to n₀"
    },
    {
      "range": {
        "end": {
          "character": 25,
          "line": 2
        },
        "start": {
          "character": 24,
          "line": 2
        }
      },
      "message": "Variable name `h` is not explicitly referenced.\n\nThe binding can be removed (if unused) or named `_` (if used implicitly).\n\nNote: This linter can be disabled with `set_option linter.unusedVariables false`"
    },
    {
      "range": {
        "end": {
          "character": 8,
          "line": 3
        },
        "start": {
          "character": 2,
          "line": 3
        }
      },
      "message": "'help h' tactic does nothing\n\nNote: This linter can be disabled with `set_option linter.unusedTactic false`"
    },
